These percentages reflect the relative importance of each paragraph in contributing to the main scientific contribution of the parent segment, which is focused on defining and addressing a novel problem (Minoria Mining). Paragraph 1 introduces the core concept and objective of Minoria mining, outlining the conditions for under-representation and prediction accuracy. It also sets up the methodological approach by discussing proxy attributes and linear projections to identify minority groups within datasets.

Paragraph 2 builds on this foundation by detailing the specifics of how unit vectors are used in the projection process, introducing Pearson's median skewness as a measure for computing skew, and explaining the challenge of identifying medians across infinite possible projections. It also hints at an efficient algorithm to be discussed later in the paper, which is crucial for addressing the problem defined earlier.

Both paragraphs are essential to understanding the Minoria mining problem; however, Paragraph 1 lays down the groundwork and introduces the main objective of the research, while Paragraph 2 delves deeper into the methodological aspects that will be used to tackle this problem. Therefore, a slightly higher percentage is assigned to Paragraph 1 as it establishes the core scientific contribution more directly.
